  "formats/narrative": "Format `narrative`: begin with the direct answer in 2-4 sentences, then these sections with `###` headings: What is in your chart, Why now (dasha), The trigger (transits), The nakshatra view, What to expect. Skip a section only if the pack has nothing for it. At most 1400 words.",
  "formats/timeline": "Format `timeline`: begin with the direct answer in 2-4 sentences naming the best window. Then this table, one row per window in date order, only windows supported by the pack:\n\n| Window | Dasha (MD-AD-PD) | Transit trigger | Indication | Watch for |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n\nThen a short \"How to read this\" paragraph covering promise (from the chart and the divisional chart), then timing, then trigger, and which layer is weakest. At most 900 words plus the table.",
